     ],
     "quote": "To handle 2D images, we reshape the image x ∈ R H×W ×C into a sequence of flattened 2D patches x p ∈ R N ×(P 2 •C) , where (H, W ) is the resolution of the original image, C is the number of channels, (P, P ) is the resolution of each image patch, and N = HW/P 2 is the resulting number of patches, which also serves as the effective input sequence length for the Transformer.",
     "grounding_status": "verified",
     "match_score": 100.0
    }
   ],
   "confidence": 0.95,
   "source": "llm"
  },
